{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/444470-chronicle-overview-ideas-advice","id":444470,"title":"Chronicle overview - ideas, advice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T10:16:40-07:00","id":444470,"title":"Chronicle overview - ideas, advice?","content":"Currently working on planning a vampire chronicle. The idea is to start off with a fairly classical political setup - there's a tyrant prince, a strict autocrat, ruling by way of superior force and because he knows the dark secrets of pretty much everyone important. <br /> <br /> And then, fairly early in the chronicle, it all comes crashing down. The prince dies - with the PCs being directly involved, preferably, because as PCs they're the most important actors of the game and all. The prince is dead. There's a revolution going on. There is no safety, for anyone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sessions 1-3: The basics of the setting are established. The PCs serve the prince, as most vampires in the city do. I try to establish the prince's rule as pretty oppressive, yet still peaceful and orderly. Noone's particularly happy with the prince, and yet it's a system that works. <br /> <br /> During Session 2-3, the prince starts putting more pressure on the PCs than normal or healthy - he demands frequent service, asks them to do things they really don't want to do; that sort of thing. It is then that they are contacted by vampires wishing to overthrow the prince. This is when things should get scary and paranoid - is this a genuine plot to depose the prince, or an attempt of the prince to identify and destroy potential usurpers? The PCs should be forced to make meaningful decisions as to where they stand. <br /> <br /> Session 4-5 is the PCs dealing with their decisions - they are in the know about a conspiracy against the prince. Do they help or hinder the prince's usurpation? <br /> <br /> During or after session 5, the prince dies; one way or another. The demise of the prince is a foregone conclusion; I kinda want the PCs to be there when it happens; they could even be the ones to kill him. Either way, circumstances will be arranged so that they will be important actors in the prince's demise. <br /> <br /> During Session 6-8, the city will essentially be a war zone, as different coteries resolve their conflicts with violence now that the prince and his hounds are out of their picture. Everything is chaos; The PCs are not on top of things; survival is their main concern. <br /> <br /> It is after this phase that the game is ported into a more sandboxy environment - there is no prince (either that, or there is more than one vampire who declares himself to be the new prince). Coteries are the basic building block of the vampiric society. Coteries are all about protection; in a city without rules and anyone to enforce them, you need a coterie to keep you safe. The PCs can, essentially, do anything they want - establish a new order, if they can pull it off; follow personal goals, anything they choose to do. <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Ideas? Advice? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:46:53-07:00","id":445653,"title":"","content":"The idea looks good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It reminded me of a premade, that has this setup as well, you might find some inspiration there. It's called &quot;Into the Void&quot; from the book &quot;Reap the Whirlwind&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4167-comedicus","name":"Comedicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4167_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:09:00-07:00","id":445695,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it looks a bit like Reap the Whirlwind except that one started <i>in media res</i> when the Prince was killed.<br /> <br /> It does seem like a solid Vampire chronicle idea. I particularly like the posibility of the conspiracy being a tool for the Prince to rout out challenegers to their authority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:19:44-07:00","id":445926,"title":"","content":"Some Thoughts about a subsequent story. The players should take an active role in re-establishing control of the City. This would be a great part to introduce new villains to help flesh things out.<ul><li>A coterie of Nomads decides to settle down in the City and mess with things. They're a members of the Sanctified or Acolytes with an eschatological belief system (think oWoD Gehenna). They demand the death of certain &quot;profligate&quot; Kindred to purify the City to prevent the upcoming Doom for a bit longer. It becomes more concerning when several of the elder Kindred start converting to their belief system as well. Will the end of the world cult overrun the City?</li> <li>A kindred (&quot;the Desperate&quot;) who lost a lot during the upheaval is looking for a way to get their way back to the top. In a desperate gambit they awaken their grandsire (who is a very powerful American Indian vampire or a very powerful elder from the old world) from torpor. This ancient vampire (&quot;The Founder&quot;) is not too happy to be woken up and is very upset over how Kindred have run the City. Perhaps the Desperate recruits the players in an attempt to piece together bits of the City's Kindred history to find where the vampire is buried, maybe he tells them why he's looking or maybe he lies. The Founder might also find a use for the players, but can they stomach his harsh ruling style?</li> <li>With the death of several powerful Kindred, a number of prime hunting grounds are up for grabs. In addition, several powerful areas of influence are also available (say the Prince had ghouled the head of a powerful local Bank or even the Chief of Police). Several other coteries are going to also stake a claim on these things. Can the players navigate the danse macabre to gain themselves more land and power?</li> </ul>If you're running the game in a smaller City, say less than 25 kindred, there's no reason the players shouldn't be able to work themselves into the City leadership if they so choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T23:33:56-07:00","id":447219,"title":"","content":"Good advice; thank you people for posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T12:35:37-07:00","id":448041,"title":"","content":"It sounds to me like you want your players to be the people that end up offing the Prince. If that is indeed the case, I'd like you to consider opening your game the same way Reap the Whirlwind does. <br /> <br /> &quot;His ghouls lay smashed like broken dolls, strewn around the room by the storm of your hungry beasts. You've penetrated his haven, you've stripped him of his defenses, and it's time to finally teach this Elder to respect his juniors. He's pushed you too far, made too many demands. The only way to make him stop is to stop him. For he is the Prince, and if he survives this night, you will not.&quot; <br /> <br /> Have the first scene of the first session be offing the Prince. It will signal to your players where you want this to go and probably will get them to help make it happen. If this idea appeals to you, I'd urge you to make the Prince a secondary character. Leave him as the archetype lurking in the background, unless he is making his demands. Make your front and center NPCs the vampires that will be the major players after the Prince's death. This will help your players prepare for that aftermath, making them actors instead of reactors following the fall out. Even better if they make an enemy or two in those pre-death nights. Then they have someone to fight during the chaos. If you build the Prince into an interesting, dynamic, deep character that the players get to know well before his death, it might lead to feeling like those sessions talking to the Prince were wasted time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1744-thantrax","name":"Thantrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}